N5008 [dcl.spec.auto]/3-4,11 + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A function template with a
DEDUCED return type (`auto` / `decltype(auto)`) whose body returns a call
containing a pack expansion (`decltype(auto) impl(seq<I...>){ return add(I...); }`).
Previously left incomplete ("could not fully type-check 'main'") because the
eager auto-return type-check ran on the unexpanded pack call; fixed by expanding
the body's call-argument packs (from the instance's pack_expr_map) before the
eager return-type deduction and body type-check.  A trailing return type over
the same call (`-> decltype(add(I...))`) was already handled
(cpp11_decltype_return_nontype_pack_call, CORE).  This is the
auto/decltype(auto)-return layer used by libstdc++'s std::apply / __apply_impl.
Non-vacuous: the returned value is a concrete function of the deduced pack.
